# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx` and `src/components/bottom-nav.module.css`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages.

- Do NOT `position: fixed` on `html`. Do NOT make `body` a flex column or `overflow-y: auto`.
- The tab bar is a **floating pill**, not a full-width flush bar. Geometry in `bottom-nav.module.css`: `position: fixed`, `left: 50%`, `transform: translateX(-50%)`, `width: 92%`, `max-width: 420px`, `height: 62px`, `border-radius: 9999px`, `bottom: calc(var(--bottom-nav-offset) - var(--kin-extra, 0px))` (offset = 20px above the **physical** screen edge, no `env()`), surface `var(--card)` with blur. `--kin-extra` is set by `useViewportCalibration` / the `viewport-init` script: it is how far the iOS Home Screen layout viewport stops short of the real screen bottom (0 in browsers). `#app-frame` extends down by the same amount (`bottom: calc(-1 * var(--kin-extra))`). Fixed elements anchored with `bottom` use `--app-chrome-bottom` (already minus extra); padding inside the frame uses `--bottom-nav-height`. Do not pin the nav with other JS. Do not add Tailwind `pb-*` / `mb-*` / `pb-safe` on the nav.
- Do NOT hide the nav on route change.

Every route uses `PageShell` with `w-full min-h-full pb-[100px] pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)] bg-background`. Home and Agenda locked shells drop that bottom padding (`padding-bottom: 0`) so content fills the viewport; the ask bar docks just above the pill. Agenda inner scrollers keep `padding-bottom: 100px` so the last row clears the pill.
`PageHeader` is not sticky.
